{
  "name": "Kit: marketing workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6b340888-9c58-4cb3-b88a-9789ff6871e0",
      "name": "Case in",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "kit-marketing",
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "marketing",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Each case comes in here",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b3f4133f-4968-416e-acee-51a78c3292b2",
      "name": "Read the rules",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        260,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "{{KIT_TOOLS_URL}}/rules/marketing/n8n/triage.md",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        }
      },
      "notes": "Reads the business rules: n8n/triage.md",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b00a9d2e-c35c-4a00-a02a-50196355de40",
      "name": "Triage",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        560,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Email:\n{{ $('Case in').item.json.body.input.email }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "={{ $('Read the rules').item.json.text }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "AI: sorts the email",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8c59aa8d-824f-4be1-bcb5-4572b50ad9c7",
      "name": "Triage model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        560,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "{{KIT_MODEL}}"
        },
        "responsesApiEnabled": true,
        "options": {
          "timeout": 100000,
          "maxRetries": 1,
          "textFormat": {
            "textOptions": {
              "type": "json_schema",
              "name": "result",
              "schema": "={{ JSON.stringify({ ...$('Case in').item.json.body.output_schema, $schema: undefined, title: undefined }) }}"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "{{OPENAI_CREDENTIAL_ID}}",
          "name": "Kit OpenAI"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "745ca2e9-64cf-44e8-8b16-a037fd9b068b",
      "name": "Read result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        840,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// The model answers JSON text, in the Response Format of its model node. Read it into `output`.\n// Also takes {\"output\": {...}} or a ```json block, so a good answer never stops the workflow.\nconst text = $json.text.trim().replace(/^```(?:json)?\\s*|\\s*```$/g, '');\nconst answer = JSON.parse(text);\nconst wrapped = answer.output && typeof answer.output === 'object' && Object.keys(answer).length === 1;\nreturn { json: { output: wrapped ? answer.output : answer } };"
      },
      "notes": "Reads the AI answer",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "id": "34736874-6510-4819-b392-3278ae776ba1",
      "name": "Result out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.output) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Sends it to the kit",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "id": "note-marketing-in",
      "name": "Note: in",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 840,
        "content": "## 1 The email comes in\nWhen you run an eval, the kit sends each test email (a **case**) to **Case in**. The email text is in `input.email`. **Read the rules** gets the business rules file `usecases/marketing/n8n/triage.md` (kit UI → **Rules**) on every case: an edit there counts from the next case, no push.\n\n**See the data of one eval case:** kit results → the case → **n8n execution ↗** → double-click a node."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-marketing-triage",
      "name": "Note: triage",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 540,
        "height": 840,
        "content": "## 2 Triage (AI)\n**The prompt** is the business rules file `n8n/triage.md` (kit UI → **Rules**); the node gets it from **Read the rules**. One model call sorts the email: category and flags.\n**Triage model** > Options > Response Format forces the result shape of the case (`output.schema.json`): a schema change needs no edit here.\n**Read result** reads the answer. Change one thing, Publish, run the eval again."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-marketing-out",
      "name": "Note: out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 840,
        "content": "## Result out\nSends the result to the kit.\nA change of the graph here (a new node): **Publish** (top right); the eval saves it to `n8n/workflow.json`."
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Case in": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Read the rules",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Read the rules": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Triage",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Triage": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Read result",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Read result": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Result out",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Triage model": {
      "ai_languageModel": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Triage",
            "type": "ai_languageModel",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "saveDataSuccessExecution": "all",
    "executionTimeout": 110,
    "binaryMode": "separate"
  }
}
